{"uuid":"AD76986A-C075-53D5-A449-A8A91439832B","name":"Honey Garlic Crockpot Shredded Chicken","serves":10,"duration":15,"cookingDuration":210,"defaultScale":1,"isPublicRecipe":false,"folderIDs":[],"ingredients":[{"uuid":"03BD226C-F126-5D15-A03D-0D9B96EFCA34","order":0,"ingredient":{"uuid":"7AFF82D7-77D1-57B2-B5BC-1F23564FA913","name":"chicken breast, whole (not cubed)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":6}},{"uuid":"8D023F03-AC09-531D-8F26-F2112492BBF9","order":1,"ingredient":{"uuid":"5BFBA7B5-A9F2-5192-8639-498E709A910A","name":"chicken broth"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"4A62047C-2EFA-52E6-87E2-516D149C9A06","order":2,"ingredient":{"uuid":"0682D755-DCA9-506E-8A23-F8F262CF1645","name":"honey"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.6667}},{"uuid":"4A0BFB00-D4E8-57F0-9A7E-A6C524ED4E91","order":3,"ingredient":{"uuid":"39CA3450-24C1-586C-B0C6-507DECD0A3FB","name":"low-sodium soy sauce"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"8A9AC34E-BB2D-580D-9D49-311533B70604","order":4,"ingredient":{"uuid":"2B5CB1FA-F0A1-5A61-892A-51DBAAF8398C","name":"cloves garlic, minced"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":9}},{"uuid":"97BB1E98-2B4E-52D8-9435-9CAD345688D8","order":5,"ingredient":{"uuid":"B83564BF-FE7E-5385-8700-931CBD5391C1","name":"butter"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":4}},{"uuid":"B4800542-7EBB-5809-B759-DFA24120DF79","order":6,"ingredient":{"uuid":"FA5434D7-DF8D-50C4-B90A-445993339862","name":"cornstarch + 3 tbsp cold water"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":1.5}},{"uuid":"24BD5B49-49FB-56A6-B81F-B3C608F294C0","order":7,"ingredient":{"uuid":"902A37BC-48F8-5E7F-B6D1-199A3AAE0B47","name":"reserved crockpot liquid"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"162B405B-F10E-5E8E-9C9F-D1344CCCCB7B","order":8,"ingredient":{"uuid":"267C762A-11EA-5C71-807F-560E0CF6869F","name":"jasmine rice (dry)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":3.5}},{"uuid":"D721B500-1124-5991-A57C-E396F471782C","order":9,"ingredient":{"uuid":"04FC00C3-48A4-5094-B42E-D43BDD9061D7","name":"fresh green beans"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":2}},{"uuid":"D56B5F23-B502-541B-B2E9-12A4A401FAA2","order":10,"ingredient":{"uuid":"98157717-03F2-541B-A1A8-6B0671BA1ABF","name":"Olive oil, salt, pepper"}}],"steps":[{"uuid":"91D4B146-F61A-5CE7-913F-BB70E1A7C9F7","order":0,"step":"Place 6 lbs whole chicken breasts in the crockpot. Season with salt and pepper and add ½ cup chicken broth for moisture. No cutting required — this is the point of the recipe.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"2817E768-3427-57AB-9964-BBA1FA9BF84B","order":1,"step":"Cook on High 3–4 hours, or Low 6–7 hours, until the chicken reaches 165°F and is fork-tender.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"1EBA3EA9-1217-519B-875C-BDAD93C99636","order":2,"step":"Drain the cooking liquid but reserve ½ cup of it. Draining prevents a watery result; the reserved half cup goes back into the sauce for volume and flavor without added sugar.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"4106F3B1-B8C7-57DD-B08E-3E4193461CE0","order":3,"step":"Shred the chicken with a hand mixer directly in the crockpot — 6 lbs takes about 30 seconds. A few pulses is enough; over-mixing turns it mushy.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"31839D4C-8A0D-5188-94F7-7C39C14DCBF6","order":4,"step":"In a saucepan, combine ⅔ cup honey, ½ cup low-sodium soy sauce, 8–9 cloves minced garlic, 4 tbsp butter, and the ½ cup reserved crockpot liquid. Simmer 3–4 minutes.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"2D43E493-F322-522C-A526-4381EF44CFBF","order":5,"step":"Taste the sauce before thickening. Low-sodium soy is noticeably less punchy than regular — add a splash more soy or a pinch of salt if it reads flat.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"1E19E003-7AAD-54BB-9462-5B018050BF54","order":6,"step":"Whisk 1 ½ tbsp cornstarch into 3 tbsp cold water, then stir the slurry into the simmering sauce. Cook 1–2 minutes until it coats the back of a spoon.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"38646A4B-6909-57CE-88C5-017A9946A277","order":7,"step":"Pour the sauce over the shredded chicken and stir. Hold on Warm for 10–15 minutes so the shredded meat absorbs it.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"8755D0A1-F5E5-5D72-A542-A97D8F4FC5D4","order":8,"step":"During the last ~20 minutes of chicken time, rinse 3 ½ cups jasmine rice until the water runs clear. Add to the Instant Pot with 3 ½ cups water. Valve on SEALING. Pressure Cook High 3 minutes, natural release 10 minutes, quick release. Fluff and cool.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"E60A8504-2B3E-5BE7-815A-2363B80E6746","order":9,"step":"Trim the green beans and toss with olive oil, salt, and pepper. Air roast at 400°F in the Ninja toaster oven for 15–18 minutes until tender with slightly crispy tips.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"63B4FA58-D809-5DC9-9413-167FCB2029F6","order":10,"step":"Cool everything 10–15 minutes. Assembly line across 10 containers: 170 g chicken, then 140 g rice, then 90 g green beans. The sauce is already in the chicken, so no separate sauce container.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"A7CAE4ED-9C19-541A-A9EE-774232A8E13B","order":11,"step":"Label with a dry-erase marker. 6 to the fridge, 4 to the freezer. Move freezer containers to the fridge the night before.","isSection":false}],"notes":"UNTESTED — v3, never cooked\nQuantities are planned, not observed. Weigh the components and update the recipe before trusting these numbers.\n\nPER CONTAINER (10 total)\n  chicken: 170 g\n  rice: 140 g\n  green beans: 90 g\n  total: 400 g\n\nTAGS: no-cutting, freezer-friendly, hands-off, scratch-sauce\n\nSTORAGE: 6 fridge, 4 freezer\nFreezer containers move to the fridge the night before eating.\n\nUNTESTED — quantities below are planned, not observed. Weigh the shredded\nchicken after step 4 and the cooked rice after step 9, then update the\nrecipe with real numbers and promote to dialed-in.\n\nSauce was scaled up from a smaller scratch recipe. Shredded chicken absorbs\nfar more sauce than cubed does, and the original ½ cup honey / ⅓ cup soy\nversion yields roughly 300 g of sauce against 6 lbs of meat — not enough.\nThe reserved crockpot liquid is what closes the volume gap without adding\nsugar. If it still reads dry after step 8, add more reserved liquid rather\nthan more honey.\n\nLow-sodium soy was chosen deliberately: Aldi does not reliably carry a\nbottled honey garlic sauce, and the bottled version runs ~25 g added sugar\nand ~1400 mg sodium per container. The scratch version should land closer\nto 17 g and 700 mg.\n\nCrockpot whole breasts retain considerably more weight than oven-cubed\nchicken, and eliminate the raw chicken cutting step entirely. Trade-off is\nno seared flavor — the sauce carries it instead.\n\nGreen beans are more forgiving than broccoli and hard to overcook.\n\nThe beans go in the Ninja toaster oven at 400°F air roast rather than the main\noven at 425°F — the fan makes up the 25°F, so the timing is unchanged. Nothing\nin this recipe needs the main oven, which leaves it free for a second prep.","neutritionalInfo":"Serving Size: 1 container,\nCalories: 600 kcal,\nProtein: 55 g,\nCarbohydrates: 65 g,\nFat: 10 g,\nFiber: 4 g,\nSodium: 700 mg,\nSugar: 17 g","sourceName":"ten-containers","webLink":"https://zjbecker32.github.io/ten-containers/recipes/honey-garlic-shredded-chicken/","tags":[],"images":[]}